// TrenchBroom units, 1 unit = 0.0254 m, floor top at z 0.
// Room interior x 0 to 512, y 0 to 384, ceiling z 256. A doorway in the south wall at x 224 to 288 opens
// onto a hallway, interior x 224 to 288, y minus 320 to minus 64, ceiling z 128, capped at its south end.
// Seam pair_door covers the hallway at y minus 256 to minus 128, targets catalog id seam-pair-a, and carries tag airlock.
// Its landmark pair_landmark stands on the hallway floor at 256 minus 192 0, yaw 90, a quarter turn from map A.
// A crossing from map A arrives walking north into this room.
// The player_spawn keyed checkpoint pair_door is the seam spawn set after a crossing.
// Every brush is an axis-aligned box. Keep comments free of braces and quotes.
